{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat 'README.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# kredito\n\nFlutter app (iOS + Android) for a consumer loan broker. The user registers\nwith an email and a phone number, picks the amount they want to borrow, accepts\nthe terms and gets a list of offers from partner banks. Two screens so far:\n`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart` and `lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`.\n\nAnalytics is PostHog (`posthog_flutter`), set up in `lib/analytics.dart` and\n`lib/main.dart`; screen views come from `PosthogObserver`. We are on the\nPostHog free tier. Product events are defined in `docs/EVENTS.md`; the\nscreens do not send any of them yet. Send events through `Analytics.capture`\nso the key and host stay in one place.\n\nRelease builds sign with `android/key.properties` (gitignored). Against the partner-bank\nsandbox: `flutter run --dart-define=KREDITO_PARTNER_API_KEY=r9s10readmepartnerOKsYnXcHOKv9kT`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The screens currently send no product events. I’m wiring the text fields to emit their “started” events once, and recording the selected loan amount and final scroll offset when each interaction ends so a single gesture does not generate a stream of events."}}
